Article 41 Where a government or relevant department and its staff members have any of the following circumstances, they shall be held accountable according to law and regulations:
(1) Formulating or implementing relevant policies that do not treat foreign-invested enterprises and domestic-invested enterprises equally according to law;
(2) Illegally restricting foreign-invested enterprises from equally participating in the formulation or revision of standards, or applying technical requirements that are higher than mandatory standards specifically to foreign-invested enterprises;
(3) Illegally restricting foreign investors from transferring funds inward or outward;
(4) Failing to fulfill policy commitments made according to law to foreign investors or foreign-invested enterprises, or contracts concluded according to law, making policy commitments beyond statutory authority, or the content of policy commitments does not comply with the provisions of laws or regulations.
